AU  - Xu, WS
AU  - Bai, YL
AU  - Wu, Y
AU  - Liu, YL
TI  - "Just using my phone to escape stress today." Daily perceived stress influences problematic mobile phone use: A daily diary study
T2  - PERSONALITY AND INDIVIDUAL DIFFERENCES
AB  - Problematic mobile phone use (PMPU) is defined as the inability to regulate mobile phone use, which has a harmful impact on physical and mental health. Previous research has identified the between-person association between perceived stress (PS) and PMPU. However, the effect of PS on PMPU in daily life remains unclear. The present study utilized a 14-day daily diary design to collect data once a day from 146 participants. We constructed a multilevel moderated mediation model to investigate the within-person relationship between daily PS and PMPU, and to examine the mediating role of daily negative emotions (NEs) and the moderating role of cognitive reappraisal (CR). Multilevel path analysis revealed that daily PS indirectly impacted daily PMPU through daily NEs. Furthermore, CR moderated the relationship between daily NEs and daily PMPU. Overall, our findings emphasize the value of alleviating daily PS and reducing daily NEs in preventing college students from developing PMPU, and highlight the complexity of CR and contribute to the expanding literature on emotion regulation.
